WEBVTT


00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.831
<i> It's been a while since I was</i>


00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.031
<i> ...up here in front of you maybe i'll stick to the cards</i>


00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:34.631
<i>There's been speculation that I was involved in the events
that occurred on the freeway and the rooftop.</i>


00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.131
<i>I'm sorry, Mr. Stark, but do you
honestly expect us to believe that</i>


00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.131
<i>that was  bodyguard
in a suit</i>


00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:43.850
<i> that conveniently appeared,
despite the fact that you historically despise bodyguards?</i>


00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.331
<i> Yes.</i>


00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.851
<i>And this mysterious bodyguard was...</i>


00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.631
<i>...somehow equipped with...</i>


00:00:50.632 --> 00:00:53.085
<i>...an undisclosed Stark high-tech
powered battle suit?</i>


00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.515
<i> I know that it's confusing.</i>


00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.031
<i>It is one thing
to question the official story</i>


00:00:58.063 --> 00:01:02.398
<i> and another thing entirely to make wild accusations
or insinuate that I'm a superhero.</i>


00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:08.108
<i>I mean, let's face it I'm not,
the heroic type.</i>


00:01:08.762 --> 00:01:11.354
<i> I've a laundry list of character defects,
all the mistakes that I've made...</i>


00:01:11.355 --> 00:01:13.328
<i>largely public.</i>


00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:14.796
<i> The truth is...</i>


00:01:19.239 --> 00:01:21.002
<i> ...I am Iron Man.</i>


00:01:25.603 --> 00:01:26.849
Ivan ...


00:01:31.215 --> 00:01:32.514
Ivan?


00:01:58.846 --> 00:02:00.306
That should be you.


00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:02.875
Do not listen to these morons.


00:02:04.967 --> 00:02:06.794
I'm sorry.


00:02:07.813 --> 00:02:11.804
I can only offer you
my knowledge.


00:04:27.172 --> 00:04:30.520
<i> Iron Man stabilizes East-West relations</i>


00:05:05.859 --> 00:05:09.258
<i> 7-0 at 30 knots.
Holding steady at 15000 feet.</i>


00:05:09.259 --> 00:05:12.096
<i>You are clear for exfiltration
over the drop zone.</i>


00:05:12.741 --> 00:05:16.248
Six months later


00:07:06.854 --> 00:07:08.635
It's good to be back!


00:07:10.203 --> 00:07:11.395
You missed me.


00:07:11.396 --> 00:07:14.172
- Blow something up!
- Blow something up?


00:07:14.196 --> 00:07:15.672
I already did that.


00:07:16.221 --> 00:07:19.718
I'm not saying that the world is enjoying...


00:07:19.719 --> 00:07:22.104
...its longest period of
uninterrupted peace in years...


00:07:22.109 --> 00:07:23.639
because of me.


00:07:26.399 --> 00:07:28.339
I'm not saying...


00:07:28.903 --> 00:07:32.112
...that from the ashes of captivity...


00:07:32.337 --> 00:07:36.477
...never has a greater Phoenix metaphor
been personified in human history.


00:07:39.545 --> 00:07:41.151
I'm not saying...


00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:45.237
...that Uncle Sam can kick back
on a lawn chair,...


00:07:45.238 --> 00:07:47.178
...sipping on iced tea,...


00:07:47.238 --> 00:07:49.878
...because I haven't come across anyone
who's man enough...


00:07:49.879 --> 00:07:52.738
...to go toe to toe with me
on my best day!


00:07:56.927 --> 00:08:00.010
- I love you Tony!
- Please. It's not about me.


00:08:01.479 --> 00:08:03.743
It's not about you.


00:08:05.403 --> 00:08:08.343
It's not even about us.
It's about legacy.


00:08:09.211 --> 00:08:12.031
It's about what we choose to leave behind
for future generations.


00:08:12.032 --> 00:08:14.113
And that's why for the next year...


00:08:14.132 --> 00:08:16.113
and for the first time since 1974,...


00:08:16.114 --> 00:08:18.110
...the best and brightest men and women


00:08:18.114 --> 00:08:20.415
...of nations and corporations the world over...


00:08:20.416 --> 00:08:23.749
will pool their resources
share their collective vision,


00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.791
to leave behind
a brighter future.


00:08:26.877 --> 00:08:28.487
It's not about us!


00:08:29.345 --> 00:08:32.399
Therefore, what I am saying,
if I'm saying anything,


00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.187
...is welcome back to the Stark Expo!


00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:42.100
Now, making a special guest appearance
from the great beyond,


00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:43.460
to tell you what it's all about,


00:08:43.662 --> 00:08:46.420
please welcome my father, Howard.


00:08:48.251 --> 00:08:50.942
<i>Everything is achievable through technology.</i>


00:08:50.951 --> 00:08:53.642
<i> Better living.
Robust health.</i>


00:08:53.643 --> 00:08:56.022
<i> And for the first time in human history,</i>


00:08:56.143 --> 00:08:58.022
<i> the possibility of world peace.</i>


00:08:58.023 --> 00:09:02.110
<i> So from all of us here at Stark Industries,
I would like to personally introduce you to</i>


00:09:02.111 --> 00:09:04.327
<i> The city of the future.</i>


00:09:04.939 --> 00:09:08.159
<i> technology holds infinite possibilities
for mankind.</i>


00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.531
Blood toxicity 19%


00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:14.738
<i> soon, technology will affect
the way you live your life every day.</i>


00:09:14.739 --> 00:09:16.548
<i> No more tedious work,</i>


00:09:16.639 --> 00:09:19.048
<i> leaving more time,
leisure activities</i>


00:09:19.283 --> 00:09:20.928
<i> and enjoying sweet life.</i>


00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.857
<i>The Stark Expo.
Welcome.</i>


00:09:28.771 --> 00:09:30.754
We are coming to you live from the kick-off
of the Stark Expo


00:09:30.771 --> 00:09:34.104
where Tony Stark
has just walked onstage.


00:09:34.105 --> 00:09:36.078
Don't worry if you can't make it down here now,


00:09:36.105 --> 00:09:38.078
because this expo goes on all year long.


00:09:38.079 --> 00:09:40.170
And I'm gonna be here checking out
all the attractions


00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:43.970
and the pavillions and the inventions
from all around the world.


00:09:44.305 --> 00:09:45.749
It's a zoo out there, watch out alright.


00:09:45.755 --> 00:09:47.479
Open up. Let's go.


00:09:47.647 --> 00:09:49.750
Nice to see you, alright.


00:09:49.757 --> 00:09:51.179
Thank you.
I remember you.


00:09:53.047 --> 00:09:54.529
- Call me.
- Hey, come on ...


00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:55.854
Hi there, dear friend.


00:09:55.855 --> 00:09:57.985
It'll be a pleasure.


00:09:58.299 --> 00:10:00.856
- See ya buddy.
- This is Larry.


00:10:00.857 --> 00:10:03.466
The oracle of goracle.
What a pleasure, nice to see you.


00:10:03.467 --> 00:10:04.861
Call me.


00:10:04.862 --> 00:10:06.009
- Larry King.
- Larry!


00:10:06.573 --> 00:10:08.926
Yes, my people, my people.


00:10:08.927 --> 00:10:11.678
- Did it go pretty mellow?
- It wasn't so bad.


00:10:11.679 --> 00:10:13.499
- No, it's perfect.


00:10:13.603 --> 00:10:15.453
Look what we got here,
the new model.


00:10:15.673 --> 00:10:17.211
- Hey, does she come with the car?
- I certainly hope so.


00:10:17.212 --> 00:10:18.478
Hi. And you are?


00:10:18.479 --> 00:10:20.451
- Marshall. - Irish. I like it.
- Pleased to meet you Tony


00:10:20.452 --> 00:10:22.300
I'm on the wheel, you mind?


00:10:22.658 --> 00:10:23.849
- Where you from?
- Bedford.


00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.185
- What are you doing here?
- Looking for you.


00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.685
Yeah? You found me.


00:10:28.426 --> 00:10:31.065
- What are you up to later?
- Serving subpoenas.


00:10:31.758 --> 00:10:33.849
Yikes.


00:10:34.015 --> 00:10:36.629
- He doesn't like to be handed things.
- Yeah I have a peeve.


00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:40.017
You are hereby ordered to appear before
the Senate Armed Services Committee


00:10:40.018 --> 00:10:41.566
tomorrow morning at 9 am.


00:10:41.567 --> 00:10:44.457
- Can I see a badge? - You wanna see the badge?
- He likes the badge.


00:10:45.537 --> 00:10:47.664
- You still like it?
- Yup.


00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:51.707
- How far are we from D.C.?
- D.C.?


00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.357
250 miles.


00:10:55.394 --> 00:10:59.157
Mr. Stark, can we pick up now
where we left off?


00:10:59.194 --> 00:11:00.607
Mr. Stark?


00:11:00.873 --> 00:11:01.985
- Please.
- Yes, dear?


00:11:01.986 --> 00:11:03.700
- Can I have your attention?
- Absolutely.


00:11:03.701 --> 00:11:06.836
Do you or do you not possess a specialized weapon?


00:11:06.837 --> 00:11:08.627
- I do not.
- You do not?


00:11:08.628 --> 00:11:12.479
- I do not, well it depends how you define
the word weapon. - The Iron Man weapon.


00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.501
My device does not fit
that description.


00:11:14.502 --> 00:11:18.879
- Well, how would you describe your..?
- I would describe it by defining it as what it is, sir.


00:11:19.267 --> 00:11:22.558
- As?
- It's a high-tech prosthesis.


00:11:23.212 --> 00:11:26.162
That is, that's actually the most apt description
I could make of it.


00:11:26.163 --> 00:11:31.096
- It's a weapon Mr Stark I hate to inform you it's a weapon.
- Please, if your priority was actually the well-being...


00:11:31.231 --> 00:11:35.746
My priority is to get the Iron Man weapon
turned over to the people of the United States of America.


00:11:35.747 --> 00:11:37.343
Well, you can forget it.


00:11:37.447 --> 00:11:41.343
I am Iron Man.
The suit and I are one.


00:11:41.344 --> 00:11:44.347
To turn over the Iron Man suit would be
to turn over myself, which is tantamount to


00:11:44.448 --> 00:11:46.105
indentured servitude or prostitution


00:11:46.248 --> 00:11:48.185
depending on what state you're in.


00:11:48.253 --> 00:11:51.368
- I can't have it.
- Look, I am no expert.


00:11:51.369 --> 00:11:53.693
In prostitution? Of course not,
you're a senator, come on!


00:11:55.961 --> 00:11:58.133
I'm not an expert in weapons.


00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:01.869
But we have somebody here who is an expert
on weapons. I would now like to call Justin Hammer


00:12:01.879 --> 00:12:05.302
Our current primary weapons contractor.


00:12:05.342 --> 00:12:09.101
Let the record reflect that I observe
Mr. Hammer entering the chamber


00:12:09.102 --> 00:12:10.391
and I am wondering...


00:12:10.392 --> 00:12:15.328
if and when any
actual expert will also be in attendance.


00:12:17.954 --> 00:12:20.150
Absolutely. I am no expert.


00:12:20.154 --> 00:12:22.079
I defer to you, Anthony.


00:12:22.046 --> 00:12:23.850
You're the wonder boy.


00:12:23.856 --> 00:12:25.620
Senator, if I may...


00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.151
I may well not be an expert,
but you know who was the expert?


00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.821
Your dad!


00:12:31.897 --> 00:12:34.982
Howard Stark.
Really a father to us all.


00:12:34.997 --> 00:12:37.582
and to the millitary-industrial age.


00:12:37.781 --> 00:12:41.742
Let's just be clear, he was no flower child.
He was a lion.


00:12:42.312 --> 00:12:43.321
We all know why we are here:


00:12:43.322 --> 00:12:45.113
In the last six months,


00:12:45.122 --> 00:12:48.813
Anthony Stark has created
a sword with untold possibilities.


00:12:48.953 --> 00:12:51.564
And yet I insists it's a shield.


00:12:51.835 --> 00:12:54.129
He asks us to trust him


00:12:54.135 --> 00:12:56.029
as we cower behind it.


00:12:56.307 --> 00:12:59.226
I wish I were comforted, Anthony.
I really do.


00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:02.200
I'd like to leave my door unlocked
when I leave the house,


00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.800
but this ain't Canada.


00:13:03.837 --> 00:13:05.400
You know we live in a world
of grave threats,


00:13:05.437 --> 00:13:09.400
threats that Mr. Stark
will not always be able to foresee.


00:13:09.981 --> 00:13:13.777
Thank you. God bless
Iron Man, God bless America.


00:13:15.662 --> 00:13:17.546
Well said, Mr. Hammer.


00:13:17.716 --> 00:13:20.156
The committee would now like to invite


00:13:20.216 --> 00:13:22.526
Lieut. Col. James Rhodes to the chamber.


00:13:22.527 --> 00:13:23.867
Rhodey?


00:13:29.721 --> 00:13:33.109
Hey, buddy. Didn't expect
to see you here.


00:13:33.119 --> 00:13:36.687
Look, it's me. I'm here. Deal with it.
Let's move on.


00:13:36.738 --> 00:13:38.173
- I just ...
- Drop it. - Alright, I'll drop it.


00:13:38.227 --> 00:13:41.627
I have before me a complete report on
the Iron Man weapon


00:13:41.727 --> 00:13:43.227
compiled by Colonel Rhodes.


00:13:43.228 --> 00:13:47.738
and Colonel, for the record,
can you please read page 57, paragraph 4?


00:13:47.739 --> 00:13:50.466
You're requesting that I read specific selections
from my report, senator?


00:13:50.467 --> 00:13:51.105
Yes, sir.


00:13:51.106 --> 00:13:55.335
My understanding that I was going to be
testifying in a much more comprehensive and detailed manner.


00:13:55.336 --> 00:13:57.079
I understand, a lot of things have changed today.


00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:00.744
You do understand that reading a single paragraph out of
context does not reflect the summary of my finding?


00:14:00.745 --> 00:14:03.411
Just read it, Colonel. I do. Thank you.


00:14:04.821 --> 00:14:06.075
Very well.


00:14:07.646 --> 00:14:11.243
As he does not operate within any
definable branch of government,


00:14:13.027 --> 00:14:16.853
The Iron Man presents a potential threat
to the security of both the nation


00:14:17.122 --> 00:14:18.390
and to her interests.


00:14:18.611 --> 00:14:23.200
I did, however, go on to summarize that the benefits
of Iron Man far outweigh the liabilities


00:14:23.263 --> 00:14:24.828
and that it would be in our interest


00:14:24.863 --> 00:14:27.828
to fold Mr Stark into the existing
chain of command.


00:14:27.829 --> 00:14:31.260
I'm not a joiner but I'll consider Secretary of
Defense, if you ask nice.


00:14:31.502 --> 00:14:33.252
We can amend the hours a little bit.


00:14:34.459 --> 00:14:38.402
I'd like to go on and show, if I may,
the imagery that's connected to your report.


00:14:38.403 --> 00:14:43.012
I believe it is somewhat premature to reveal
these images to the general public at this time.


00:14:43.099 --> 00:14:46.100
With all due respect, Colonel, I understand.
And if you could just narrate those for us,


00:14:46.199 --> 00:14:47.900
we'd be very grateful.


00:14:48.567 --> 00:14:49.749
Show the images.


00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.635
Intelligence suggests that the
devices seen in these photos


00:14:54.636 --> 00:14:57.104
are in fact attempts at making manned copies


00:14:57.136 --> 00:14:59.154
of Mr. Stark's suit.


00:14:59.155 --> 00:15:02.104
This has been corroborated by our allies


00:15:02.155 --> 00:15:03.774
and local intelligence on the ground


00:15:03.775 --> 00:15:06.099
indicating that these suits are


00:15:06.175 --> 00:15:08.999
quite possibly at this moment operational.


00:15:09.403 --> 00:15:11.038
Hold on a second buddy, let me see.


00:15:11.999 --> 00:15:14.186
There's something here.
Oh, boy I'm good.


00:15:14.199 --> 00:15:16.086
Now can I get more screens.


00:15:16.971 --> 00:15:19.846
I need them.
Time for a little transparency.


00:15:19.895 --> 00:15:21.662
- Let's see what's really going on.
- What is he doing?


00:15:21.663 --> 00:15:24.155
If you'll direct your attention to said screens,


00:15:24.163 --> 00:15:26.655
I believe that's North Korea.


00:15:35.331 --> 00:15:37.050
Can you turn that off? Take it off.


00:15:37.051 --> 00:15:38.992
Iran.


00:15:41.398 --> 00:15:44.144
No grave, immediate threat here.


00:15:44.198 --> 00:15:46.044
Is that Justin Hammer?


00:15:46.188 --> 00:15:48.621
How did Hammer get in here?


00:15:48.622 --> 00:15:50.511
Justin, you're on TV, focus up.


00:16:01.494 --> 00:16:05.567
Wow. Yeah, I'd say most countries, 5-10 years away.


00:16:05.646 --> 00:16:09.497
- Hammer Industries 20.
- I'd like to point out that that test pilot survived.


00:16:09.498 --> 00:16:12.614
I think we got the point that he's making.
I don't think there's any reason...


00:16:12.698 --> 00:16:14.214
The point is you're welcome, I guess.


00:16:14.215 --> 00:16:16.706
- For what?
- Because, I'm your nuclear deterrent.


00:16:17.007 --> 00:16:19.178
It's working. We're safe.
America is secure.


00:16:19.207 --> 00:16:21.278
You want my property?
You can't have it!


00:16:21.279 --> 00:16:23.376
But did I you a big favor.


00:16:23.379 --> 00:16:25.946
I've successfully privatized world peace.


00:16:28.929 --> 00:16:30.309
What more do you want?


00:16:30.728 --> 00:16:32.005
For now!


00:16:32.601 --> 00:16:35.309
I'm tired of all of these ass clowns!


00:16:35.761 --> 00:16:38.190
Fuck you Mr Stark.
Fuck you buddy.


00:16:38.714 --> 00:16:40.924
- We're adjourned, we're adjourned for today.
- Okay


00:16:41.248 --> 00:16:42.916
You've been a delight.


00:16:48.258 --> 00:16:50.167
<i> My bond is with the people.</i>


00:16:50.355 --> 00:16:52.324
<i> And I will serve this great nation</i>


00:16:52.355 --> 00:16:55.884
<i> at the pleasure of myself.</i>


00:16:56.183 --> 00:16:59.071
<i> One thing I've proven
is that you can count on me ...</i>


00:16:59.386 --> 00:17:00.611
<i> ...to pleasure myself.</i>


00:17:34.661 --> 00:17:37.610
- Wake up, daddy's home.
- Welcome home, sir.


00:17:37.694 --> 00:17:40.254
Congratulations on the opening ceremonies.
They were such a success.


00:17:40.294 --> 00:17:42.274
as was your Senate hearing.


00:17:42.619 --> 00:17:47.154
And may I say how refreshing it is to finally
see you in a video with your clothing on, sir?


00:17:50.061 --> 00:17:51.330
You!


00:17:51.862 --> 00:17:55.234
I swear to god I'll dismantle you, I'll switch
your motherboard and turn you into wine rack.


00:17:56.992 --> 00:17:59.968
How many ounces a day of this gargle
am I supposed to drink?


00:17:59.969 --> 00:18:03.510
We are up to 80 ounces a day
to counteract the symptoms, sir.


00:18:04.908 --> 00:18:06.608
Check palladium levels.


00:18:08.699 --> 00:18:11.168
Blood toxicity: 24%


00:18:12.212 --> 00:18:16.367
It appears that the continued use of the
Iron Man suit is accelerating your condition.


00:18:18.372 --> 00:18:20.383
Another core has been depleted.


00:18:23.988 --> 00:18:25.432
God, they're running out quick.


00:18:25.667 --> 00:18:28.041
I have run simulations
on every known element


00:18:28.042 --> 00:18:31.503
and none can serve as a viable replacement for
the palladium core.


00:18:34.331 --> 00:18:36.486
You are running out of both time
and options.


00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:44.631
Unfortunately, the device
that's keeping you alive, is also killing you.


00:18:46.565 --> 00:18:49.389
Ms. Potts is approaching.
I recommended that you inform her of...


00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.618
Mute.


00:18:53.894 --> 00:18:55.138
Is this a joke?


00:18:56.708 --> 00:18:57.873
What are you thinking?


00:18:57.908 --> 00:18:59.450
- What?
- What are you thinking?


00:18:59.492 --> 00:19:02.519
Hey, I'm thinking I'm busy
and you're angry about something.


00:19:02.989 --> 00:19:04.345
Do you have the sniffles? I don't wanna get sick.
Keep your distance


00:19:04.346 --> 00:19:08.831
Did you just donate our entire
modern art collection to the...


00:19:09.301 --> 00:19:11.100
- Boy Scouts of America?
- Yes it is a...


00:19:11.101 --> 00:19:12.802
worthwhile organization.


00:19:12.803 --> 00:19:16.025
I didn't physically check the crates,
but basically yes.


00:19:16.026 --> 00:19:18.169
And it's not our collection, it's my collection. No offense.


00:19:18.268 --> 00:19:21.759
No, you know what I think I'm actually entitled to say
Our collection,


00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:25.792
considering the time that I've put in
over 10 years curating that.


00:19:25.793 --> 00:19:26.985
It's a tax write-off, I needed that.


00:19:26.986 --> 00:19:29.159
You know, there's only about 8,011 things


00:19:29.186 --> 00:19:31.859
that I really need to talk to you about.


00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:34.783
