- Trust me I know I'm good at this stuff.


01:01:26.176 --> 01:01:28.511
I've been looking for a suitable replacement
for palladium.


01:01:28.512 --> 01:01:32.256
I've tried every combination, every permutation of
every known element.


01:01:32.332 --> 01:01:35.675
Well, I'm here to tell you
you haven't tried them all.


01:01:37.145 --> 01:01:39.846
Hey, hey, hey.
Special delivery.


01:01:40.064 --> 01:01:41.431
Candygram!


01:01:45.111 --> 01:01:47.269
I brought you something.


01:01:51.533 --> 01:01:54.651
- We got you the bird, pal.
- This is not my bird.


01:01:55.036 --> 01:01:58.235
What do you mean?
That's the bird.


01:01:58.236 --> 01:01:59.864
I pulled a lot of strings
to get this bird.


01:01:59.915 --> 01:02:02.167
- It's a great bird.
- It's a beautiful bird.


01:02:02.168 --> 01:02:06.412
- We got this all the way from Russia.
- Hey man, it's not my bird.


01:02:08.298 --> 01:02:12.459
Well listen, even if it's not the bird,
I mean this is a gorgeous bird.


01:02:12.552 --> 01:02:16.254
I mean, look, don't get so attached to
things, learn to let go.


01:02:19.225 --> 01:02:21.884
Wait a minute.
Jack, what is that?


01:02:22.102 --> 01:02:25.179
Is that...
That's not a helmet. What is that?


01:02:33.238 --> 01:02:36.815
Ivan... What's this?
Jack?


01:02:37.575 --> 01:02:42.069
Is that a helmet? It doesn't look like a helmet
to me. How are you supposed to get a head in there?


01:02:42.162 --> 01:02:45.199
- Jack, could you put your head in there? - No.
- Try to put your head in there.


01:02:45.200 --> 01:02:46.991
Go ahead, try to put your head in there.


01:02:47.084 --> 01:02:49.535
See Ivan, he can't put his head in
there. That's...


01:02:49.920 --> 01:02:52.108
That's not a helmet, it's a head.


01:02:52.120 --> 01:02:53.498
I need to put a guy in there.


01:02:53.499 --> 01:02:57.333
I need to fit a person
in that suit, you understand?


01:02:57.593 --> 01:02:58.668
Drone better.


01:02:58.719 --> 01:03:00.418
What? Drone better?
Why is drone better?


01:03:00.419 --> 01:03:02.263
Why drone better?


01:03:02.264 --> 01:03:04.108
People make problem.


01:03:04.164 --> 01:03:06.008
Trust me,
drone better.


01:03:06.393 --> 01:03:10.596
Ivan, you know I like you.
I got you the bird.


01:03:11.147 --> 01:03:15.725
You said no problem.
That's what you said to me, you said no problem.


01:03:15.818 --> 01:03:18.612
Now I need suits.
The government wants suits.


01:03:18.613 --> 01:03:20.572
Like Iron Man, you understand?


01:03:20.573 --> 01:03:23.858
That's what the people want.
That's what's gonna make them happy.


01:03:24.368 --> 01:03:25.860
Hey, man...


01:03:27.120 --> 01:03:30.105
Don't get to attached to things.


01:03:30.120 --> 01:03:31.865
Learn to let go.


01:03:35.086 --> 01:03:38.296
These drones better steal the show, Ivan.


01:03:38.297 --> 01:03:41.916
You understand? They better
rock my world, Ivan.


01:03:51.017 --> 01:03:52.801
Unbelievable.


01:03:53.019 --> 01:03:55.637
This ought to get the Senate off my ass.


01:03:55.730 --> 01:03:59.057
- It's functional?
- Fully mission-capable.


01:03:59.191 --> 01:04:02.185
Good. Get Hammer down here
to weaponize it.


01:04:03.329 --> 01:04:04.237
Sir?


01:04:04.238 --> 01:04:07.109
Justin Hammer's making a weapons presentation
at the expo.


01:04:07.138 --> 01:04:08.699
We'd like this to introduce it.


01:04:08.700 --> 01:04:10.201
Sir, I don't believe that the expo is...


01:04:10.202 --> 01:04:13.111
Colonel, the world needs
to see this fast.


01:04:13.246 --> 01:04:14.830
We've got to make this happen.


01:04:14.831 --> 01:04:17.907
- Yes general, but the...
- It's also an order.


01:04:18.334 --> 01:04:19.742
Yes, sir.


01:04:19.919 --> 01:04:22.787
Good work, Colonel.
You've made your country proud.


01:04:23.464 --> 01:04:25.081
Thank you, sir.


01:04:30.971 --> 01:04:34.506
That thing in your chest is
based on unfinished technology.


01:04:34.682 --> 01:04:37.343
No it was finished,
it's never been particularly effective until


01:04:37.344 --> 01:04:40.261
I've miniaturized it
and put it in my...


01:04:40.438 --> 01:04:43.542
No, Howard said that the arc reactor was
a stepping stone to something greater.


01:04:43.643 --> 01:04:45.102
He was about to kick off an energy race


01:04:45.143 --> 01:04:48.102
That was gonna dwarf
the arms race.


01:04:48.278 --> 01:04:51.363
He was on to something big,
something so big


01:04:51.364 --> 01:04:54.900
that it was gonna make the nuclear reactor
look like a AAA battery.


01:04:54.909 --> 01:04:57.244
Just him? Or was Anton Vanko in on this too?


01:04:57.245 --> 01:05:00.405
Anton Vanko is the other
side of that coin.


01:05:00.414 --> 01:05:02.596
Anton saw it as a
way to get rich.


01:05:02.597 --> 01:05:04.917
When your father found
out he had him deported.


01:05:04.918 --> 01:05:08.421
When the Russians found out he couldn't
deliver they shipped his ass off to Siberia


01:05:08.422 --> 01:05:11.090
and he spent the next 20 years on a vodka
fuel rage.


01:05:11.091 --> 01:05:13.542
Not quite the environment you wanna raise
a kid in.


01:05:13.635 --> 01:05:17.545
His son you had the misfortune of
crossing paths with in Monaco.


01:05:17.930 --> 01:05:20.102
You told me I hadn't tried everything.
What do you mean I haven't tried everything?


01:05:20.130 --> 01:05:21.632
What haven't I tried?


01:05:21.633 --> 01:05:25.302
He said that you were the only person with the
means and knowledge


01:05:25.521 --> 01:05:27.554
to finish what he started.


01:05:27.564 --> 01:05:28.889
He said that?


01:05:29.107 --> 01:05:31.391
Are you that guy?
Huh? Are you?


01:05:31.693 --> 01:05:37.313
Because if you are then
you can solve the riddle of your heart.


01:05:40.868 --> 01:05:44.537
I don't know where you get your information, but
he wasn't my biggest fan.


01:05:44.538 --> 01:05:47.449
- What do your remember about your dad huh?
- He was cold, he was calculating...


01:05:47.450 --> 01:05:50.376
He never told me he loved me
he never even told me he liked me.


01:05:50.377 --> 01:05:54.796
So it's a little tough for me to digest what're you telling
me he said the whole future is riding on me


01:05:54.797 --> 01:05:57.123
and he's passing it down...
I don't get that.


01:05:57.425 --> 01:05:58.793
We're talking about a guy
whose happiest day


01:05:58.794 --> 01:06:00.293
was when he shipped me off to boarding school.


01:06:00.328 --> 01:06:01.386
That's not true.


01:06:01.387 --> 01:06:03.796
Well, then clearly you know my dad better
than I did.


01:06:04.056 --> 01:06:06.041
As a matter of fact I did.


01:06:06.156 --> 01:06:07.841
He was one of the founding members
of The Shield.


01:06:07.893 --> 01:06:10.638
- What?
- I got a two o'clock.


01:06:10.639 --> 01:06:12.396
Wait, wait, what's this?


01:06:12.397 --> 01:06:14.189
- Okay, you're good, right?
- No I'm not good.


01:06:14.190 --> 01:06:17.058
- You got this, right? - Got what? I don't
even know what I'm supposed to get.


01:06:17.110 --> 01:06:20.153
Natasha will remain
a floater at Stark with her cover intact


01:06:20.154 --> 01:06:22.100
and you remember
Agent Colson right?


01:06:22.102 --> 01:06:23.515
Yeah.


01:06:23.582 --> 01:06:24.815
Oh, and Tony...


01:06:25.826 --> 01:06:28.861
Remember, I got my eye on you.


01:06:34.626 --> 01:06:37.101
We've disabled all communications,
no contact with the outside world.


01:06:37.126 --> 01:06:38.861
Good luck.


01:06:43.092 --> 01:06:44.842
Please...


01:06:44.843 --> 01:06:48.054
First thing I need a little body work.
I'll put in a little time at the lab.


01:06:48.055 --> 01:06:52.558
If you could send of your goon squad down to the Coffee Bean
across the street or Starbucks, that'll be nice.


01:06:52.559 --> 01:06:55.095
I'm not here for that.
I've been authorized by


01:06:55.096 --> 01:06:57.771
Director Fury to use any means necessary
to keep you on premises.


01:06:57.772 --> 01:07:00.398
- If you attempt to leave - Right
- or play any games


01:07:00.399 --> 01:07:01.733
I will taze you and watch


01:07:01.734 --> 01:07:03.476
Supernanny while you
drool into the carpet. Okay?


01:07:03.902 --> 01:07:07.229
- I think I got it, yeah.
- Enjoy your evening's entertainment.


01:07:32.762 --> 01:07:34.513
Think this
is the power source?


01:07:34.514 --> 01:07:37.304
Major, this is not a scientific exercise.


01:07:37.314 --> 01:07:39.384
Let's just focus
on arming it, alright?


01:07:40.214 --> 01:07:41.895
Yes, sir.


01:07:41.896 --> 01:07:43.262
<i> Oh, yes!</i>


01:07:43.564 --> 01:07:45.431
Oh, yes, yes, yes!


01:07:45.482 --> 01:07:47.391
Is it my birthday?


01:07:47.442 --> 01:07:50.811
You gotta.. what did you do?
What did you do?


01:07:53.656 --> 01:07:56.232
- Is this what I think it is?
- Yes it is.


01:07:56.667 --> 01:07:59.702
Hammer, I want to know
what you're gonna do for us.


01:07:59.878 --> 01:08:01.840
What am I gonna do for you?


01:08:01.878 --> 01:08:04.540
First thing I'm gonna do for you is
I'm gonna upgrade your software,


01:08:07.078 --> 01:08:10.140
I'm talking about firepower.


01:08:11.489 --> 01:08:13.522
Well you're talking to the right guy.


01:08:14.350 --> 01:08:17.593
Claridge Hi-Tec semi-automatic 9 mm pistol.


01:08:18.771 --> 01:08:21.055
Too downtown?
I agree.


01:08:21.482 --> 01:08:23.849
M-24 shotgun pump action.


01:08:24.234 --> 01:08:26.770
5-round magazine, but
you know what, you're not a hunter.


01:08:26.771 --> 01:08:28.755
What am I talking about?
I'm getting rid of it.


01:08:28.771 --> 01:08:31.455
This is the FN-2000 from Belgium.


01:08:31.456 --> 01:08:33.149
They do make something better than waffles.


01:08:34.202 --> 01:08:36.501
It's beautiful, but I can tell this isn't
disco enough for you


01:08:36.502 --> 01:08:37.954
so I'm gonna put it right here.


01:08:37.955 --> 01:08:42.369
You're looking at a Milkor 40 mm grenade launcher.
Tear gas, smoke.


01:08:42.370 --> 01:08:44.649
Hippie control.
You're tough.


01:08:44.650 --> 01:08:47.459
Let me tell you something,
Size does matter.


01:08:47.460 --> 01:08:49.214
Don't let anyone tell you different.


01:08:49.370 --> 01:08:54.009
This is an M134 7.62 minigun.
Six individual barrels.


01:08:54.010 --> 01:08:56.334
The torso taker, powder maker.


01:08:56.370 --> 01:09:00.014
Our boys in uniform call it Uncle Gazpacho
or Puff the Magic Dragon.


01:09:03.170 --> 01:09:04.334
Okay.


01:09:06.050 --> 01:09:09.774
These are the Cubans baby.
These are the Cohibas, the Montecristos...


01:09:11.090 --> 01:09:13.249
That's a kinetic-kill sidewinder vehicle


01:09:13.250 --> 01:09:17.294
with a secondary cyclotrimethylenetrinitramine
RDX burst.


01:09:17.890 --> 01:09:21.329
It's capable of busting a bunker under
the bunker you just busted.


01:09:21.330 --> 01:09:23.249
If it were any smarter it would write a book.


01:09:23.250 --> 01:09:26.459
A book that would make Ulysses look like
it was written in crayon.


01:09:26.960 --> 01:09:28.574
And would read it to you.


01:09:29.290 --> 01:09:32.729
This is my Eiffel Tower,
This is my Rachmaninoff's Third.


01:09:32.730 --> 01:09:36.574
My Pieta. It's completely
elegant, it's bafflingly beautiful.


01:09:36.810 --> 01:09:41.014
And it's capable of reducing the population
of any standing structure to zero.


01:09:42.290 --> 01:09:44.694
I call it the Ex-Wife.


01:09:49.090 --> 01:09:50.854
That's the best I got.


01:09:55.650 --> 01:09:58.404
How are you gonna do this? Give me something.
You're like a sphinx.


01:09:58.450 --> 01:09:59.894
I can't read you.


01:10:00.370 --> 01:10:01.569
I think I'll take it.


01:10:01.570 --> 01:10:04.094
- Which one?
- All of it.


01:10:05.970 --> 01:10:07.254
All of it?


01:10:38.810 --> 01:10:39.934
<i>Action.</i>


01:10:42.970 --> 01:10:46.669
<i>Everything is achievable through technology.</i>


01:10:46.670 --> 01:10:48.894
<i>Better living,
robust health.</i>


01:10:49.090 --> 01:10:52.374
<i>And for the first time
in human history...</i>


01:10:52.410 --> 01:10:55.014
<i>the possibility of world peace.</i>


01:10:55.210 --> 01:10:58.509
<i>I'm Howard Stark. And everything
you'll need for the future,</i>


01:10:58.510 --> 01:10:59.974
<i>can be found right here.</i>


01:11:00.170 --> 01:11:04.014
<i> City of Future, City of
of Tomorrow? Hang on.</i>


01:11:08.730 --> 01:11:10.049
<i>I'm Howard Stark.</i>


01:11:10.050 --> 01:11:12.934
<i> And everything you'll need in
the future can be found right here.</i>


01:11:13.690 --> 01:11:18.214
<i> So, from all of us in
Stark Industries I would like to personally...</i>


01:11:19.330 --> 01:11:21.409
<i> Tony? What are you doing back there?
What is that?</i>


01:11:21.410 --> 01:11:24.254
<i>Put it back.
Put it back where you got it from.</i>


01:11:25.250 --> 01:11:27.094
<i>Where is your mother?
Maria...</i>


01:11:27.610 --> 01:11:29.814
<i>Go on, go, go, go...</i>


01:11:31.650 --> 01:11:33.454
<i>Sorry I think we got the...</i>


01:11:34.170 --> 01:11:36.414
<i>I'll come in in there...</i>


01:11:39.970 --> 01:11:41.674
<i>Are you waiting on me?</i>


01:11:43.250 --> 01:11:47.254
<i>So from all of us in
Stark Industries I'd like to personally show you...</i>


01:11:48.490 --> 01:11:49.569
<i> my ass.</i>


01:11:49.570 --> 01:11:53.974
<i>I'd like to... This...
I can't... We have this don't we?</i>


01:11:54.050 --> 01:11:56.414
<i>That looks ridiculous.</i>


01:11:57.330 --> 01:11:58.614
<i>Everything...</i>


01:11:59.730 --> 01:12:01.414
<i>is achievable...</i>


01:12:02.050 --> 01:12:03.254
<i>through technology.</i>


01:12:15.570 --> 01:12:17.009
<i>Tony...</i>


01:12:17.010 --> 01:12:21.094
<i>You're too young to understand this right now
so I thought I would put it on film for you.</i>


01:12:23.290 --> 01:12:25.294
<i> I built this for you.</i>


01:12:26.130 --> 01:12:30.534
<i> And someday you'll realize that it represents
a whole lot more than just people's inventions.</i>


01:12:30.970 --> 01:12:32.934
<i>It represents my life's work.</i>


01:12:33.610 --> 01:12:35.774
<i>This is key to the future.</i>


01:12:38.770 --> 01:12:41.254
<i>I'm limited by the technology
of my time.</i>


01:12:41.690 --> 01:12:43.654
<i> But one day you'll figure this out.</i>


01:12:43.970 --> 01:12:48.294
<i>And when you do...
you will change the world.</i>


01:12:49.970 --> 01:12:54.094
<i> What is and always will be
my greatest creation...</i>


01:12:56.010 --> 01:12:57.614
<i>is you.</i>


01:13:16.450 --> 01:13:17.809
Hi, sir.


01:13:17.810 --> 01:13:20.509
- $6.
- I don't have any...


01:13:20.510 --> 01:13:23.214
- No sir, that's too much.
- No it's fine, take that.


01:13:25.770 --> 01:13:27.234
Take it, take it.


01:13:27.470 --> 01:13:30.234
I don't like people hand me things so if you
could just drop that there that would be great.


01:13:30.530 --> 01:13:32.774
- Are you Iron Man?
- Sometimes.


01:13:33.010 --> 01:13:34.574
We believe in you!


01:13:35.050 --> 01:13:37.734
It was an illegal seizure
of trademarked property.


01:13:37.770 --> 01:13:40.249
- Ms. Potts, Mr Stark is...
- Here.


01:13:40.250 --> 01:13:43.374
- He refuses to...
- I don't. It's fine. I'll just be a second.


01:13:43.730 --> 01:13:49.294
It's our position that Stark has the means to maintain
proprietary ownership of the Mark II platform.


01:13:49.690 --> 01:13:52.449
<i>When Mr. Stark announced he was the Iron Man</i>


01:13:52.450 --> 01:13:56.489
<i>he was making a promise to America.</i>


01:13:56.490 --> 01:13:58.414
<i>Obviously he did not.</i>


01:13:58.650 --> 01:14:00.594
<i>Now we learn that his secretary,</i>


01:14:00.650 --> 01:14:03.094
<i>a woman named
Virginia "Pepper" Potts,</i>


01:14:03.170 --> 01:14:05.409
<i>has been appointed CEO
of Stark Industries executive.</i>


01:14:05.470 --> 01:14:07.609
<i>What are her qualifications?</i>


01:14:07.610 --> 01:14:08.209
No.


01:14:08.210 --> 01:14:10.574
- Ms. Potts is doing nothing to manage the terrible
situation... - Mute.


01:14:11.970 --> 01:14:16.529
Bert, don't tell me that we have the
best patent lawyers in the country


01:14:16.530 --> 01:14:18.254
and then not let me pursue this.


01:14:18.850 --> 01:14:19.889
I'll get this stuff out of here.


01:14:19.890 --> 01:14:21.934
Well then, tell the President
to sign an order.


01:14:23.210 --> 01:14:25.404
We'll talk about it at the expo.


01:14:25.410 --> 01:14:27.534
Hammer's giving some presentation
tomorrow evening.


01:14:27.810 --> 01:14:31.169
- Will Tony Stark be there?
- Will I?


01:14:31.170 --> 01:14:33.094
- No, he will not.
- I'd like to be.


01:14:34.530 --> 01:14:35.769
- Got a minute?
- No.


01:14:35.770 --> 01:14:37.814
Come on, you just got off the phone.
30 seconds.


01:14:40.490 --> 01:14:42.694
29 ... 28 ...


01:14:42.890 --> 01:14:47.094
I was driving over here, and I thought
I was coming basically to apologize, but I'm not.


01:14:47.170 --> 01:14:50.974
- You didn't come here to apologize?
- That goes without saying, and I'm working on that.


01:14:51.210 --> 01:14:54.809
But I haven't been entirely up front
with you


01:14:54.810 --> 01:14:56.409
and I just wanna try to make good,


01:14:56.410 --> 01:14:59.729
Can I move this?
This is crazy I got ferris wheel...


01:14:59.730 --> 01:15:00.894
No.


01:15:03.690 --> 01:15:05.454
Do you know how short life is?


01:15:06.010 --> 01:15:08.889
And if I never got to express...


01:15:08.890 --> 01:15:11.649
and by the way somewhat revelatory to me,


01:15:11.650 --> 01:15:14.349
I don't care... I mean, I care, it would be nice,


01:15:14.350 --> 01:15:17.094
I'm not expecting you to...
Look, here's what I'm trying to say.


01:15:17.490 --> 01:15:20.289
Let me just stop you right here, okay,
because if you say "I"


01:15:20.290 --> 01:15:23.534
one more time, I'm gonna actually hurl
something at your head, I think.


01:15:24.530 --> 01:15:28.129
I am trying to run a company.
Do you know have any idea what that entails?


01:15:28.130 --> 01:15:28.974
Yes.


01:15:29.050 --> 01:15:31.889
People are relying on you to be
Iron Man, and you've disappeared.


01:15:31.890 --> 01:15:35.134
All I'm doing is putting out your fire
and taking the heat for it.


01:15:37.610 --> 01:15:41.174
I am trying to do the job that you
were meant to do.


01:15:44.530 --> 01:15:46.374
Did you bring me strawberries?


01:15:47.650 --> 01:15:51.724
Did you know that there is only one thing
on earth that I am allergic to?


01:15:51.725 --> 01:15:52.849
You're allergic to strawberries, uh-uh.


01:15:55.650 --> 01:15:59.214
This is progress, Pepper. I knew there
was correlation between you and this...


01:16:00.290 --> 01:16:02.374
- I need you...
- And I need you too, that's what I'm trying to say.


01:16:02.450 --> 01:16:04.854
to leave now.


01:16:09.250 --> 01:16:10.374
Ms Potts.


01:16:11.090 --> 01:16:14.414
- Hi, come on in.
- Wheel's up in 25 minutes.


01:16:14.770 --> 01:16:16.274
Thank you.


01:16:17.890 --> 01:16:18.929
Anything else, boss?


01:16:18.930 --> 01:16:22.414
- I'm good Hap.
- I'll be just... another minute.


01:16:23.370 --> 01:16:25.214
I lost both the kids in the divorce.


01:16:28.970 --> 01:16:30.114
No.


01:16:32.170 --> 01:16:34.854
Are you blending in well here, Natalie?


01:16:35.090 --> 01:16:37.454
Here at Stark... Enterprises.


01:16:38.050 --> 01:16:39.654
Your name is Natalie, isn't it?


01:16:40.330 --> 01:16:43.529
I thought you two
didn't get along.


01:16:43.530 --> 01:16:45.854
- No, that's not so.
- It's just me you don't care for.


01:16:46.570 --> 01:16:47.649
No? Nothing?


01:16:47.650 --> 01:16:51.764
Actually while you're here maybe you and Natalie
could discuss the matter of personal belonging.


01:16:51.765 --> 01:16:52.894
Absolutely.


01:16:59.570 --> 01:17:03.649
- I'm surprised you could keep your mouth shut.
- You're good. You are mind-blowingly duplicitous.


01:17:03.650 --> 01:17:04.459
How do you do it?


01:17:04.460 --> 01:17:07.114
You're a triple impostor.
I've never seen anything like it.


01:17:07.160 --> 01:17:09.114
Is there anything real about you?
Do you even speak Latin?


01:17:09.115 --> 01:17:11.209
Fallaces sunt rerum species.


01:17:11.215 --> 01:17:14.039
Which means?
What did you just say?


01:17:14.040 --> 01:17:16.724
It means you can either drive yourself home
or I can have you collected.


01:17:18.760 --> 01:17:20.164
You're good!


01:18:17.360 --> 01:18:20.204
Jarvis, could you kindly
backform a digital wireframe?


01:18:20.260 --> 01:18:21.804
I need a manipulable projection.


01:18:29.720 --> 01:18:32.884
1974 Stark Expo model scanning
complete, sir.


01:18:34.840 --> 01:18:39.204
- How many buildings are there?
- Am I to include the Belgian waffles stand?


01:18:39.400 --> 01:18:41.324
It was rhetorical, just show me.


01:18:53.640 --> 01:18:55.604
What does that look like to you, Jarvis?


01:18:56.360 --> 01:18:58.124
Not unlike an atom.


01:18:58.360 --> 01:19:02.124
In which case, the nucleus... would be here.


01:19:02.960 --> 01:19:04.404
Highlight the Unisphere.


01:19:12.940 --> 01:19:18.004
- Notice the footpaths. Get rid of them.
- What is it you're trying to achieve, sir?


01:19:18.360 --> 01:19:21.484
I'm discovering,... correction, rediscovering...


01:19:22.480 --> 01:19:23.724
... a new element.


01:19:24.840 --> 01:19:27.999
Lose the landscape and the shrubbery there,
trees,


01:19:28.000 --> 01:19:29.884
parking lots, exits, entrances.


01:19:34.120 --> 01:19:36.604
Structre protons and neutrons


01:19:36.760 --> 01:19:40.284
using flags the pavillions as the framework.


01:20:04.200 --> 01:20:06.444
Dead for almost 20 years...


01:20:07.840 --> 01:20:09.804
...still taking me to school.


01:20:14.920 --> 01:20:19.444
The proposed element should serve
as a viable replacement for palladium.


01:20:19.920 --> 01:20:21.039
Thanks, Dad.


01:20:21.040 --> 01:20:23.884
Unfortunately,
it is impossible to synthesize.


01:20:27.920 --> 01:20:31.644
Get ready for major remodel, fellas!
We're back in hardware mode.


01:21:17.280 --> 01:21:19.614
How did you break the perimeter?


01:21:19.680 --> 01:21:21.714
That was like three years ago.
Where have you been?


01:21:21.715 --> 01:21:24.804
- I was doing some stuff.
- Yeah, well, me too and it worked.


01:21:26.240 --> 01:21:30.279
Hey, I'm playing for the home team, Colson
You and all your Fabulous Furry Freak Brothers.


01:21:30.280 --> 01:21:32.124
Let me work, or break my balls?


01:21:33.640 --> 01:21:34.924
What's this doing here?


01:21:37.600 --> 01:21:38.844
That's it.


01:21:39.360 --> 01:21:40.804
Bring it to me.


01:21:41.120 --> 01:21:43.444
- You know what this is?
- It's exactly what I need to make this work.


01:21:45.140 --> 01:21:46.444
Lift the coil.


01:21:46.360 --> 01:21:49.284
Go, go! Put your knees under it.
There you go.


01:21:49.320 --> 01:21:50.684
And...


01:21:51.400 --> 01:21:53.244
- Drop it. - Okay.


01:21:56.440 --> 01:21:57.484
Perfectly level.


01:21:58.320 --> 01:22:00.284
- I'm busy. What do you want?
- Nothing.


01:22:00.320 --> 01:22:02.884
Good bye. I've been reassigned.


01:22:03.000 --> 01:22:04.519
Director Fury wants me in New Mexico.


01:22:04.520 --> 01:22:07.204
- Fantastic, the land of enchantment.
- So I'm told.


01:22:07.240 --> 01:22:08.924
- Secret stuff.
- Something like that.


01:22:10.320 --> 01:22:11.404
- Good luck.
- Bye.


01:22:11.880 --> 01:22:13.479
- Thanks.
- We need you.


01:22:13.480 --> 01:22:16.084
- Yeah, more than you know.
- Not that much.


01:22:33.720 --> 01:22:35.964
<i>Initializing
prismatic accelerator.</i>


01:22:42.160 --> 01:22:44.604
<i>Approaching maximum power.</i>


01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.324
That was easy.


01:23:47.020 --> 01:23:48.844
<i>Congratulations, sir.</i>


01:23:50.480 --> 01:23:52.724
<i>You have created a new element.</i>


01:24:00.460 --> 01:24:03.844
<i>Sir, the reactor has accepted the
modified core.</i>


01:24:04.480 --> 01:24:06.524
<i>I will begin running diagnostics.</i>


01:24:12.280 --> 01:24:13.964
Hey, Ivan.


01:24:14.400 --> 01:24:18.399
<i>I got Senator Stern here. Thought we'd swing over
and look at some of the drone designs.</i>


01:24:18.100 --> 01:24:21.804
- The drone is not going to be ready.
- Not ready... What do you mean?


01:24:22.320 --> 01:24:25.244
It can make presentation
not demonstration.


01:24:25.320 --> 01:24:30.084
- What the hell is the difference?
- Presentation, no fly, no shoot.


01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:33.204
Wait. What can we make 'em do, I mean,


01:24:33.260 --> 01:24:35.004
This is a weapons demonstration.


01:24:35.120 --> 01:24:36.684
I can make salute.


01:24:37.160 --> 01:24:39.644
You can make salute, what do you mean
make salute?


01:24:39.800 --> 01:24:41.644
What the hell does that mean, Ivan?


01:24:41.920 --> 01:24:44.204
<i>It's not what we agreed to, okay.</i>


01:24:44.220 --> 01:24:46.754
<i>You promised me suits, and then you promised
me drones.</i>


01:24:46.755 --> 01:24:50.484
- Hey man, everything will be okay.
- This is not what I wanted.


01:25:02.040 --> 01:25:04.684
Hey, there he is, the bird man.


01:25:06.760 --> 01:25:08.604
Oh, now you like the bird, is that right?


01:25:08.760 --> 01:25:11.804
Is that your bird?
I'm confused.


01:25:12.400 --> 01:25:15.644
You said it wasn't, but now
it's like you're best of pals.


01:25:15.840 --> 01:25:17.244
You love that bird, don't you?


01:25:17.960 --> 01:25:19.564
You know what? Take the bird.


01:25:24.520 --> 01:25:26.924
Take his pillows too. Both of them.


01:25:27.800 --> 01:25:29.564
And shoes, take his shoes.


01:25:33.760 --> 01:25:35.244
I took your stuff.


01:25:35.680 --> 01:25:38.684
How does that make you feel?
You feel bad?


01:25:39.200 --> 01:25:42.044
Good. Cause that's how I feel!


01:25:43.680 --> 01:25:45.604
We had a contract!


01:25:45.800 --> 01:25:50.644
I saved your life
and you give me suits.


01:25:50.920 --> 01:25:54.444
That was our deal.
And you did not deliver.


01:25:55.400 --> 01:25:58.204
I don't know if you're a genius
or a fraud.


01:25:58.210 --> 01:26:00.044
I don't know what you are!


01:26:01.960 --> 01:26:05.044
Something really, really great fell into my lap.


01:26:05.880 --> 01:26:08.884
If it hadn't, I'd be at your mercy tonight.


01:26:09.080 --> 01:26:12.959
Now I have a piece of Stark tech, and I pimped
out myself.


01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:17.199
Now your overpriced paperweights are gonna
look like a backdrop to my demonstration.


01:26:17.200 --> 01:26:19.484
You dig what I'm gettin' at here?


01:26:21.840 --> 01:26:26.004
I don't know if you noticed,
but I don't speak Russian!


01:26:29.320 --> 01:26:34.284
I'm gonna leave now. I'm gonna go to the expo.
Maybe I'll even get laid.


01:26:35.040 --> 01:26:38.844
See these guys? They're your babysitters.
They are not to be trifled with.


01:26:39.800 --> 01:26:43.124
When I get back, we're gonna renegotiate the
terms of our agreement.


01:26:44.280 --> 01:26:46.639
And you're gonna make good on our arrangements.


01:26:46.640 --> 01:26:49.204
Because if you don't, you're gonna be exactly what you were
when I found you,


01:26:49.240 --> 01:26:51.564
a dead man.


01:26:51.920 --> 01:26:53.284
You got that?


01:26:54.200 --> 01:26:56.404
Maybe you can watch me on TV.


01:27:05.220 --> 01:27:07.564
Dummy. You.
Can we clean up this mess?


01:27:08.200 --> 01:27:12.200
- Incoming call with a blocked number, sir.
- Phone privileges reinstated.


01:27:12.210 --> 01:27:13.804
Lovely.


01:27:14.040 --> 01:27:18.524
- Colson, how's land of enchantment?
- Hey, Tony, how you doin'?


01:27:19.680 --> 01:27:21.244
- I doubled cycle. - You what?


01:27:22.320 --> 01:27:26.559
You told me double cycle's
more power. Good advice.


01:27:26.560 --> 01:27:30.044
- You sound pretty spitely for a dead guy.
- You too.


01:27:32.200 --> 01:27:33.199
- Trace it. - Sir.


01:27:33.200 --> 01:27:37.524
Now the true history of
Stark name will be written.


01:27:37.560 --> 01:27:40.444
- Jarvis, where he is?
- Accessing the Oracle grid.


01:27:41.040 --> 01:27:42.444
Eastern seaboard.


01:27:42.560 --> 01:27:46.444
What your father did to my family
over 40 years


01:27:47.160 --> 01:27:49.519
I will do to you in 40 minutes.


01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:51.879
Sounds good, let's get together
and hash it out.


01:27:51.880 --> 01:27:55.444
Tri-state area.
Manhattan and outlying boroughs.


01:27:55.640 --> 01:27:57.364
I hope you're ready.


01:28:00.120 --> 01:28:01.884
<i>Call trace incomplete.</i>


01:28:12.160 --> 01:28:14.684
- Sir.
- You wanna run some tests, run 'em.


01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:17.799
And assemble the suit while you're at it
put it together now.


01:28:17.800 --> 01:28:20.164
- We are unclear as to the effects...
- I don't wanna hear it, Jarvis!


01:28:24.160 --> 01:28:27.364
It tastes like coconut...
and metal.


01:28:41.380 --> 01:28:44.804
I'll keep the car down here, alright.
- Thank you Happy.


01:28:44.820 --> 01:28:50.164
<i>Justin Hammer, his presentation will begin shortly
in the main pavilion.</i>


01:29:09.360 --> 01:29:12.284
That's what I'm talking about!
Thanks for coming.


01:29:13.400 --> 01:29:16.324
Ladies and gentlemen,
for far too long


01:29:16.800 --> 01:29:19.804
this country has had to place its brave men
and women in harm's way.


01:29:20.080 --> 01:29:22.224
But then the Iron Man arrived
and we thought that


01:29:22.280 --> 01:29:24.724
the days of losing lives were behind us.


01:29:25.880 --> 01:29:28.204
Sadly that technology was kept out of reach.


01:29:28.280 --> 01:29:30.604
That's not fair. That's not right.


01:29:30.920 --> 01:29:33.159
- And it's just too bad.
- Oh, lord...


01:29:33.160 --> 01:29:37.924
Regardless it was an impressive innovation
one that grabbed headlines the world over.


01:29:38.360 --> 01:29:43.324
Today, my friends, the press
is faced with quite a different problem.


01:29:43.920 --> 01:29:47.084
They are about to run out of ink.


01:29:51.720 --> 01:29:53.004
Get that out of here.


01:29:54.440 --> 01:29:56.164
Ladies and gentlemen...


01:29:57.120 --> 01:29:59.124
...today I present to you


01:29:59.600 --> 01:30:02.924
...the new face of the United States military!


01:30:03.920 --> 01:30:05.564
The Hammer drone!


01:30:07.740 --> 01:30:09.764
Army!


01:30:21.380 --> 01:30:26.084
Navy!


01:30:32.380 --> 01:30:35.004
Air Force!


01:30:41.100 --> 01:30:43.844
Marines!


01:30:59.700 --> 01:31:02.944
That's a hell of a lot better than some
cheerleaders, let me tell you.


01:31:04.160 --> 01:31:06.764
But as revolutionary
as this technology is,


01:31:06.800 --> 01:31:10.484
there will always be a need for a man
to be present at the theater of war.


01:31:10.880 --> 01:31:15.794
Ladies and gentlemen, today I am proud
to present to you the very first prototype


01:31:15.795 --> 01:31:19.500
the variable threat response battle suit


01:31:19.510 --> 01:31:22.644
and its pilot Air Force Lt. Col. James Rhodes.


01:31:23.550 --> 01:31:25.098
What?


01:31:45.050 --> 01:31:48.098
For America and its allies,
Hammer Industries, is reporting...


01:32:04.950 --> 01:32:06.869
We got trouble.


01:32:06.870 --> 01:32:08.789
Tony, there are civilians present.


01:32:08.790 --> 01:32:11.224
I'm here on orders.
Let's not do this right now.


01:32:11.225 --> 01:32:13.718
Give them a wave.


01:32:14.210 --> 01:32:16.404
All these people are in danger.
We gotta get them out of here.


01:32:16.405 --> 01:32:18.564
You gotta trust
me for the next five minutes.


01:32:18.565 --> 01:32:20.484
I tried that and
I got tossed around your house, remember?


01:32:20.485 --> 01:32:22.849
I think he's working with Vanko.


01:32:22.850 --> 01:32:25.898
Vanko is alive?


01:32:26.450 --> 01:32:28.884
- Where is he?
- What?


01:32:28.885 --> 01:32:30.529
Where is Vanko?


01:32:30.530 --> 01:32:32.724
- Who?
- Tell me.


01:32:32.725 --> 01:32:35.498
What are you doing here, man?


01:32:39.830 --> 01:32:43.009
- Is that you?
- No, I'm not doing that, it's not me.


01:32:43.010 --> 01:32:46.058
I can't move.
I'm locked up, I'm locked up.


01:32:46.450 --> 01:32:49.729
Get out of here! Go!
The whole system's been compromised!


01:32:49.730 --> 01:32:52.738
Let's take it outside.


01:33:03.130 --> 01:33:06.178
No!


01:33:13.890 --> 01:33:16.738
- Jarvis, break in, I need to own him.
- Yes, sir.


01:33:19.450 --> 01:33:22.029
Tony, I'm locked on I have target locked.


01:33:22.030 --> 01:33:25.378
- On what?
- On you.


01:33:28.590 --> 01:33:30.908
Tony on your six.


01:33:46.290 --> 01:33:49.169
- What's going on, what's happening?
- The software's been overwritten.


01:33:49.170 --> 01:33:51.089
What?
What do you mean it's been overwritten?


01:33:51.090 --> 01:33:53.524
- I think he slaved the drones.
- It is impossible.


01:33:53.525 --> 01:33:54.929
- Call the guards
- All the phones are down, sir.


01:33:54.930 --> 01:33:57.809
- Then call their cells.
- Their cell phones are not working either, sir.


01:33:57.810 --> 01:34:00.689
- He's locked us out of the mainframe.
- Who's locked you out of the mainframe?


01:34:00.690 --> 01:34:03.124
Please, please, go away.
I got this handled.


01:34:03.125 --> 01:34:04.529
- Have you now?
- Yes I do.


01:34:04.530 --> 01:34:06.449
In fact, if your guy hadn't showed up


01:34:06.450 --> 01:34:08.884
This wouldn't be happening
Please now, go away!


01:34:08.885 --> 01:34:10.289
Thank you.


01:34:10.290 --> 01:34:13.129
Listen we gotta get these bitches outta here.


01:34:13.130 --> 01:34:15.264
You're gonna tell me who's behind
this.


01:34:15.265 --> 01:34:16.969
Who's behind this?


01:34:16.970 --> 01:34:19.449
Ivan. Ivan Vanko.


01:34:19.850 --> 01:34:22.394
- Where is he?
- He's at my facility.


01:34:25.650 --> 01:34:28.904
- I need NYPD please.
- No, no, no honey.


01:34:28.950 --> 01:34:30.054
Don't call the authorities!


01:34:30.170 --> 01:34:32.734
Step aside.


01:34:33.290 --> 01:34:34.814
Tell me everything you know. Go.


01:34:41.890 --> 01:34:45.334
- How we doing Jarvis?
- Remote reboot unsuccessful.


01:35:03.810 --> 01:35:07.809
- No one's answering the phone, what's going on?
- Get in the car. Take me to Hammer Industries.


01:35:07.810 --> 01:35:09.129
I'm not taking you anywhere.


01:35:09.130 --> 01:35:12.334
- Fine. You want me to drive?
- No, I'm driving. Get in the car.


01:36:08.810 --> 01:36:10.334
Nice work, kid.


01:36:12.010 --> 01:36:15.254
- You got multiples coming down on you.
- Let's get this away from the expo.


01:36:20.370 --> 01:36:22.904
When we arrive I need you to watch the perimeter.


01:36:22.970 --> 01:36:25.094
I'm gonna enter the facility and take down the target.


01:36:28.530 --> 01:36:30.014
- Watch the road.
- I got it.


01:37:00.330 --> 01:37:03.209
Listen, listen, a pack has peeled off and headed
back to the expo.


01:37:03.210 --> 01:37:04.334
Got it.


01:37:08.290 --> 01:37:12.174
I'm closing on you!
It's coming in hot, Tony! Watch it.


01:37:26.930 --> 01:37:29.694
- Stay in the car!
- I'm not staying in the car.


01:37:29.970 --> 01:37:32.574
- I said stay in the car.
- What are you wearing?


01:37:35.010 --> 01:37:36.454
Look, I'm not letting you go in there alone.


01:37:37.010 --> 01:37:39.494
- You wanna help? Keep the car running.
- Okay.


01:37:43.170 --> 01:37:45.214
Hey, you can't come in here!


01:38:29.650 --> 01:38:32.769
Each set of drones
is communicating in its own unique language.


01:38:32.770 --> 01:38:36.574
- Choose one and focus on that.
- Have you tried Russian? Why don't you try Russian.


01:39:24.290 --> 01:39:25.614
I got 'em!


01:39:39.730 --> 01:39:41.334
- Rhodey, you're still locked on? - Yeah.


01:39:41.570 --> 01:39:45.414
Drop your socks and grab your
crocs, we're about to get wet on this ride.


01:39:47.170 --> 01:39:48.774
Wait, wait!


01:40:06.770 --> 01:40:08.214
He's gone!


01:40:12.690 --> 01:40:15.054
Sorry buddy, had
to thin out the herd.


01:40:15.190 --> 01:40:16.754
What's your twenty?


01:40:28.090 --> 01:40:30.894
- What are you doing?
- I'm rebooting Rhodey's suit.


01:40:37.170 --> 01:40:38.214
Tony!


01:40:53.930 --> 01:40:55.174
Reboot complete.


01:40:56.010 --> 01:40:59.449
- You got your best friend back.
- Thank you very much, Agent Romanoff.


01:40:59.450 --> 01:41:04.654
Well done with the new chest-piece. I'm reading significantly
higher output and your vitals all look promising.


01:41:04.850 --> 01:41:06.614
Yes, for the moment I'm not dying. Thank you.


01:41:07.570 --> 01:41:09.904
- What do you mean you're not dying? Did you say you're dying?
- That you?


01:41:09.970 --> 01:41:11.694
No, I'm not. Not anymore.


01:41:11.890 --> 01:41:14.009
- What's going on?
- I was going to tell you. I didn't want to..


01:41:14.010 --> 01:41:16.969
- You're gonna tell me you really were dying?
- You didn't let me.


01:41:16.970 --> 01:41:20.609
- Why didn't you tell me that?
- I was gonna make you an omelette and tell you!


01:41:20.610 --> 01:41:23.909
Hey, hey, save it for the honeymoon.
You got incoming, Tony.


01:41:23.910 --> 01:41:25.329
Looks like the fight's coming to you.


01:41:25.330 --> 01:41:27.009
- Great. Pepper?
- Are you okay now?


01:41:27.010 --> 01:41:29.769
- I'm fine. Don't be mad. I will formally...
- I am mad.


01:41:29.770 --> 01:41:32.534
...apologize when I'm not fending off a Hammeroid attack!


01:41:33.410 --> 01:41:35.454
- We could've been in Venice.
- Oh, please...


01:41:37.810 --> 01:41:39.094
Rhodes!


01:41:39.730 --> 01:41:41.374
Snap out of it, buddy!
I need you.


01:41:43.130 --> 01:41:44.614
They're coming. Come on let's roll. Get up.


01:41:48.410 --> 01:41:50.294
Oh man, you can have your suit back.


01:41:53.770 --> 01:41:56.294
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, thanks.


01:41:58.370 --> 01:42:01.269
- Tony, look... I'm sorry.
- Don't be.


01:42:01.270 --> 01:42:03.454
- No I should've trusted you more.
- I'm the one who put you in this position. Forget it.


01:42:03.890 --> 01:42:05.829
No it's your fault. I just wanted
to say I'm sorry.


01:42:05.830 --> 01:42:08.694
Thank you.
That's all I want to hear, partner.


01:42:09.250 --> 01:42:12.414
They're coming in hot. Any
second. What's the play?


01:42:13.410 --> 01:42:15.909
Well we wanna take the high ground, okay.
So let's take


01:42:15.910 --> 01:42:18.909
the biggest gun up on that ridge. - Got you.


01:42:18.910 --> 01:42:20.929
- Where do you wanna be?
- Where you going? - What are you talking about?


01:42:20.930 --> 01:42:23.209
- I mean me.
- I have a big gun, you are not the big gun.


01:42:23.210 --> 01:42:25.564
- Tony, don't be jealous.
- No it's subtle with all the bells and whistles.


01:42:25.565 --> 01:42:27.934
- It's called being a bad ass.
- Fine.


01:42:29.130 --> 01:42:32.904
- Alright. You go up top. I'll draw 'em in.
- But don't stay down here


01:42:32.930 --> 01:42:34.524
it's the worst place to be.


01:42:34.530 --> 01:42:38.514
- Okay you got a spot. Where's mine?
- It's the kill box, Tony, okay, this is where you go to die.


01:43:26.250 --> 01:43:27.774
- See that?
- Yea, yea, nice.


01:43:35.130 --> 01:43:36.134
Rhodey...


01:43:37.690 --> 01:43:38.694
Get down!


01:43:49.210 --> 01:43:51.609
Wow. I think you should lead with that
next time.


01:43:51.610 --> 01:43:55.254
Yeah, sorry boss, I can only use it once.
It's a one-off.


01:43:57.130 --> 01:43:58.854
I told you that five minutes ago.


01:44:00.410 --> 01:44:01.934
That's your guy here.


01:44:03.090 --> 01:44:04.694
- Excuse me?
- Sir, you're placed under arrest.


01:44:04.970 --> 01:44:06.449
Hands behind your back, sir.


01:44:06.450 --> 01:44:07.774
I'm trying to help here.


01:44:11.970 --> 01:44:15.414
I get it. I see what you're doing. Trying
to pin this on me, huh?


01:44:15.650 --> 01:44:19.804
That's good. You start to think like a CEO.
Taking out the competition.


01:44:19.805 --> 01:44:22.949
I like that.
You think you're making a problem for me?


01:44:22.950 --> 01:44:26.014
I'm gonna make a problem for you.
I'm gonna be seeing you again, real soon.


01:44:30.690 --> 01:44:34.454
When they get here, I think you should station them
at the Southeast and both West exits.


01:44:34.970 --> 01:44:36.729
We shut down the seven train in and out of
Willets Point already.


01:44:36.730 --> 01:44:39.734
Well, have city buses there to ferry people
to operating lines.


01:44:40.130 --> 01:44:41.489
You coming with us?


01:44:41.490 --> 01:44:43.334
No, I'm gonna stay until the park is clear.


01:44:46.250 --> 01:44:50.314
Heads up you got one more drone incoming.
This one looks different.


01:44:50.650 --> 01:44:52.854
Repulsor signature
is significantly higher.


01:45:03.330 --> 01:45:04.854
Good to be back.


01:45:05.810 --> 01:45:07.134
This ain't gonna be good.


01:45:10.370 --> 01:45:14.414
I got something special for this guy.
I'm gonna bust his bunker with the ex-wife.


01:45:14.570 --> 01:45:15.654
The what?


01:45:26.090 --> 01:45:28.294
- Hammer tech?
- Yeah.


01:45:30.090 --> 01:45:31.214
We got this.


01:46:22.250 --> 01:46:24.014
Rhodes! I got an idea.


01:46:24.900 --> 01:46:26.649
You wanna be a hero?


01:46:26.650 --> 01:46:29.289
- What?
- I can really use a sidekick.


01:46:29.290 --> 01:46:32.084
- Put your hand up.
- This is your idea?


01:46:32.085 --> 01:46:35.494
- Yup.
- I'm ready, I'm ready, go go go.


01:46:39.130 --> 01:46:40.694
Hit him!


01:47:07.250 --> 01:47:09.054
You lose.


01:47:15.990 --> 01:47:18.634
All these drones are rigged to blow
We gotta get out of here man.


01:47:18.990 --> 01:47:20.474
Pepper?


01:47:58.510 --> 01:48:00.469
Oh my god, I can't take this anymore!


01:48:00.470 --> 01:48:01.589
- You can't?
- I can't take this.


01:48:01.590 --> 01:48:02.889
What do you mean, look at me!


01:48:02.890 --> 01:48:06.864
My body literally cannot handle the stress.
I never know if you're gonna kill yourself...


01:48:06.865 --> 01:48:08.749
or wreck the whole company...


01:48:08.750 --> 01:48:10.954
I think I did okay!


01:48:11.270 --> 01:48:13.149
I quit.
I'm resigning.


01:48:13.450 --> 01:48:15.409
That's it.


01:48:15.410 --> 01:48:18.409
What did you just say?
You're done?


01:48:18.710 --> 01:48:20.869
Surprising, I mean not
surprising.


01:48:20.870 --> 01:48:24.629
I get it.
You don't have to make any excuses.


01:48:24.630 --> 01:48:26.909
- I'm not making any excuses.
- Well you actually were just making excuses.


01:48:26.910 --> 01:48:30.314
I wasn't making an excuse but I'm actually very justified.


01:48:30.410 --> 01:48:32.114
You deserve better.


01:48:32.750 --> 01:48:34.794
You've taken such good care of me.


01:48:35.950 --> 01:48:38.094
I've been in tough spot
you got me through it, so.


01:48:38.150 --> 01:48:40.269
- Right?
- Thank you.


01:48:40.270 --> 01:48:43.509
- Yeah.
- Thank you for understanding.


01:48:43.510 --> 01:48:45.924
- Let's start clean up.
- I'll handle the transition. It'll be smooth.


01:48:45.925 --> 01:48:48.389
What about the press?
Because you only had the job for a week. That's gonna be...


01:48:48.390 --> 01:48:51.314
- With you it's like dog years.
- I know.


01:48:51.590 --> 01:48:52.914
I mean it's like the President.


01:49:04.430 --> 01:49:05.914
Weird.


01:49:05.930 --> 01:49:07.114
No it's not weird.


01:49:07.170 --> 01:49:09.649
- It's okay, right?
- Yeah.


01:49:09.650 --> 01:49:12.189
I think it was weird.


01:49:12.190 --> 01:49:15.449
You guys look like two seals fighting over a grape.


01:49:15.450 --> 01:49:18.889
- I had just quit
- You don't have to do that.


01:49:18.890 --> 01:49:20.444
- I heard the whole thing.
- You should get lost.


01:49:20.445 --> 01:49:22.849
I was here first.
Get a roof.


01:49:22.850 --> 01:49:25.849
- I thought you were out of one-liners?
- That's the last one.


01:49:25.850 --> 01:49:28.414
- You kicked ass back there, by the way.
- Thank you. You too.


01:49:28.630 --> 01:49:31.429
Listen, my car got taken out in the explosions


01:49:31.430 --> 01:49:34.429
so I'm gonna have to hang on to your suit for a minute, okay?


01:49:34.430 --> 01:49:36.609
Not okay with thats.


01:49:36.610 --> 01:49:40.614
It wasn't a question.


01:49:44.910 --> 01:49:46.614
I don't understand...


01:50:05.050 --> 01:50:07.729
I don't think I want you looking at that.


01:50:07.730 --> 01:50:10.294
I'm not sure it pertains to you anymore.


01:50:10.430 --> 01:50:16.194
Now this, on the other hand, is agent
Romanoff's assessment of you.


01:50:16.470 --> 01:50:18.734
Read it.


01:50:18.870 --> 01:50:22.934
Personality overview:
Mr Stark displays compulsive behavior.


01:50:23.090 --> 01:50:25.674
In my own defense, that
was last week.


01:50:27.450 --> 01:50:30.814
Prone to self-destructive tendencies.
I was dying.


01:50:30.890 --> 01:50:33.389
I mean, please, aren't we all?


01:50:33.390 --> 01:50:36.574
Textbook narcissism?


01:50:37.290 --> 01:50:39.654
Agreed.


01:50:41.210 --> 01:50:44.389
Recruitment assessment for Avenger Initiative,
Iron Man, yes.


01:50:44.390 --> 01:50:46.854
- I gotta think about it.
- Read on.


01:50:49.570 --> 01:50:52.774
Tony Stark not recommended?


01:50:53.490 --> 01:50:57.214
That doesn't make any sense. How can
you approve me but not approve me?


01:50:58.390 --> 01:51:03.374
I got a new ticker, I'm trying to do right
by Pepper.


01:51:03.390 --> 01:51:06.969
I'm in a stable-ish relationship.


01:51:06.970 --> 01:51:12.054
Which leads us to believe at this juncture
we'd only like to use you as a consultant.


01:51:17.890 --> 01:51:20.574
You can't afford me.


01:51:22.690 --> 01:51:25.489
Then again I will waive my customary retainer


01:51:25.490 --> 01:51:28.014
in exchange for a small favor.


01:51:28.910 --> 01:51:31.409
Rhodey and I are being honored in Washington


01:51:31.410 --> 01:51:33.854
and we need a presenter.


01:51:35.430 --> 01:51:36.914
I'll see what I can do.


01:51:38.330 --> 01:51:40.409
It is my honor to be here today


01:51:40.410 --> 01:51:44.889
to present these distinguished awards
to Lt. Col. James Rhodes


01:51:44.890 --> 01:51:48.514
and Mr. Tony Stark
who is of course


01:51:48.530 --> 01:51:50.934
a national treasure.


01:51:52.250 --> 01:51:55.969
Thank you Lieutenant Colonel
for such an exceptionally distinguished performance.


01:51:55.970 --> 01:51:58.934
- You deserve this.
- Thank you, sir.


01:52:00.010 --> 01:52:05.014
Mr Stark, thank you for
such an exceptionally distinguished performance.


01:52:05.130 --> 01:52:06.754
You deserve this.


01:52:07.430 --> 01:52:09.895
Oh sorry.


01:52:10.730 --> 01:52:14.654
Funny how annoying a little prick can be, isn't it?


01:52:14.930 --> 01:52:16.454
Let's get a photo.
